:: Meeting VehVeh 1a {"position":"6150,1650","size":"100,100"}
{=

(metadata:
"NPC", "VehVeh",
"title", "Meeting Veh-Veh",
"cardDesc", "It's good to know another student here, especially the friendly sort.",)

$cssColumnParent[

$cssColumnChild[
	$cssBox[
    	($funcImage: (passage: "npc.VehVeh")'s img)
         $cssBoxItem[''(print: (passage:)'s title )''<br>(print: (passage:)'s cardDesc)]
    ]
]

$cssColumnChild[
<!--begin-->
She looks up at you. Her eyes go wide.
<br>
["Oh wow. Are you..."]<VehVehLine|
<br>
($funcInnerConvo: (dm:
     "<!--A-->\"A magus? A //davehmar//? Why, yes!\"", "1a",
     "<!--B-->\"A visitor. I came from the heartlands.\"", "1b",
))
<br>

<!--1a-->
[
["I could tell,"]<VehVehLine| she points to the star her forehead. You have one too. ["I meant... you're a //journeyman//. I've never actually met one before. Wow."]<VehVehLine|
<br>
You start to have the distinct feeling that you're being studied.
<br>
(show: ?1end)
](1a|

<!--1b-->
[
Back home, "heartland" strictly refers to the capital and its surrounds, but in Askava, "heartland" is a good enough term to say "not here".
<br>
["Of course, you're not a local,"]<VehVehLine| she cranes her head, studying you like you were a strange bird. ["There's so few magi on this island. I hardly get to meet anyone new."]<VehVehLine|
<br>
(show: ?1end)
](1b|

<!--1end-->
[
["Oh, I'm being rude. Sorry. I'm Vehk- I mean, I'm Veh-Veh. Please, call me Veh-Veh,"]<VehVehLine| she stands up and bows. What an odd name. ["I'm a student-assistant at Apesai Davehkhan."]<VehVehLine|
<br>
($funcInnerConvo: (dm:
     "<!--A-->\"An honor, Veh-Veh.\" Bow and introduce yourself.", "2b",
     "<!--B-->\"Apesai 'Davehkhan'? I wasn't aware that Apesai had a //university//.\"", "2a",
))
<br>
](1end|

<!--2a-->
[
["It doesn't. Ours isn't quite a 'university' yet, but well, there's no harm in being aspirational, right?"]<VehVehLine|
<br>
Informal teaching circles are everywhere, but only land grants by the emperor and assent from the collective davehmars will qualify a university.
<br>
["It's alright if you're not impressed. I've heard that imperial schools can get pretty... //fancy//,"]<VehVehLine| she flourishes with her fingers. ["Which school did you go to? Oh, sorry, I haven't even asked for your name!"]<VehVehLine|
<br>
($funcInnerConvo: (dm:
     "<!--A-->\"It's alright, I'm...\" Introduce yourself.", "2b",
))
<br>
](2a|

<!--2b-->
[
You tell her who you are and where you graduated from.
<br>
["So '(print: $char's player's customName)' the journeyman from Bakho university,"]<VehVehLine| she mutters, repeating your words.
<br>
Yes, you're currently journeying for employment and studying to create a Sacred Opal, as all journeymen are tasked.
<br>
Veh-Veh nods and points to the top of the lighthouse, where the aurora is emanating from.
<br>
["//That's// a Sacred Opal. A whole big //motherlode// of it, making light all by itself without any fuel or machinery. Impressive, right?"]<VehVehLine|
<br>
She makes it sound as if she had anything to do with it herself.
<br>
($funcInnerConvo: (dm:
     "<!--A-->\"Yes it is. Uhm, did you help make it or something?", "3a",
     "<!--B-->\"Ah, if only I could grab it, run back home, and submit it as my graduating thesis.\"", "3b",
     "<!--C-->\"If you study hard, you'll make one before I do.\"", "3c",
))
<br>
](2b|

<!--3a-->
[
Veh-Veh snorts and giggles.
<br>
["Haha, would I be here talking to you if that's something I could do?"]<VehVehLine| But then, she goes quiet. ["Well, it //is// a grandmaster's job to greet a journeyman if one ever comes around, so who knows?"]<VehVehLine|
<br>
She thumbs her book, seriously thinking about it.
<br>
(t8n: "dissolve")(show:?3end)
](3a|

<!--3b-->
[
["Heh, funny. The children say the same thing when I tell them about how they'd have to journey,"]<VehVehLine| she says, barely concealing her judgment. ["Then, I tell them about the defense and proof process, and what happens to plagiarists, and they quickly give up the idea. Smart kids."]<VehVehLine|
<br>
You've seen a public "admonishment" of plagiarists once. It smelled awful. The Reclaimer Emperors are very much interested in //also// reclaiming the sanctity of academia, on top of all the former territories.
<br>
["But, you know, if someone //did// manage to steal and transport Apesai's Opal, then any council would be impressed enough to certify the thief. What a feat that would be..."]<VehVehLine|
<br>
($funcInnerConvo: (dm:
     "<!--A-->\"Yeah, I suppose.", "3b1",
     "<!--B-->\"That would be a dark day.\"", "3b2",
))
<br>
](3b|

<!--3b1-->
[
["But then, we'd have a boom in increasingly complex heists and a crisis of academic integrity. Oh, Veh-Veh, what have you done..."]<VehVehLine| she continues muttering, lost in hypotheticals.
<br>
(t8n: "dissolve")(show:?3end)
](3b1|

<!--3b2-->
[
["Yes, well, it wouldn't be so bad. Most of the municipal lamps in Apesai run on vehzin anyway, and maybe we'd even get to see the night stars again, so..."]<VehVehLine| she continues muttering, lost in hypotheticals.
<br>
(t8n: "dissolve")(show:?3end)
](3b2|

<!--3c-->
[
["Ha, what are you, my teacher?"]<VehVehLine| She clears her throat and composes herself. ["Sorry, I meant to say that my teachers all say the same thing, that I'd soon be a master. I know they want to encourage me. I've already done the imperial exam twice, but there hasn't been a decision on whether I'll journey yet. Are they afraid that they won't be able to find a new assistant? No, I shouldn't think ill of them."]<VehVehLine|
<br>
($funcInnerConvo: (dm:
     "<!--A-->\"If you had a choice, hypothetically speaking, where would you go?", "3c1",
     "<!--B-->\"I hope they find you a spot soon.\"", "3c2",
))
<br>
](3c|

<!--3c1-->
[
["Nudankhan, of course. Who wouldn't want to study in the 'Capital of Magic' if it's just a matter of hypotheticals?"]<VehVehLine| She sighs. ["Failing that, I suppose Esora is fine, too. They've got big observatories, I've read that somewhere. Esorans aren't called 'star-gazers' for nothing, right? Or does that mean something else?"]<VehVehLine|
<br>
The more she goes on, the more she seems to run up against the limits of her knowledge of places outside of Askava, or even Apesai. "Star-gazers" when applied to Esorans is like "hut-dweller" here in Askava.
<br>
(t8n: "dissolve")(show:?3end)
](3c1|

<!--3c2-->
[
["Or I can just get up and leave, right? There has been 'outsider masters' before, hasn't there? Not many, but not zero. I can travel to Nudankhan, or maybe Esora, find my own mentors, then... Ugh, but the children - //someone// has to look after them, and what about traveling stipend? Without a school's sanction..."]<VehVehLine|
<br>
She stammers and fidgets with her book. You seem to have touched a sore spot.
<br>
(t8n: "dissolve")(show:?3end)
](3c2|

<!--3end-->
[
["I'm sorry, I'm talking to myself again. Bad habit. So, journeyman, is there something I can help you with?"]<VehVehLine|
<br>
($funcInnerConvo: (dm:
     "<!--A-->\"Yes, there is something I need to talk to a davehmar about.\"", "talk",
     "<!--B-->\"No, I just wanted to say hello.\"", "exit",
))
<br>
](3end|


<!--talk-->
[
["Go ahead!"]<VehVehLine|
<br>
---
<ol>
($funcNPCTopics: "Veh-Veh seems distracted. You should leave her be for today.", "\"Actually, never mind. It's good to have met a fellow student, Veh-Veh. Bye.\"")
</ol>
](talk|

<!--exit-->
[
["Alright, come by the lighthouse if you need anything, //if// I'm not downtown running errands, that is."]<VehVehLine|
<br>
---
(link: "Sure, goodbye Veh-Veh. It's good to have met a fellow student.")[$funcBack]
](exit|

